translate english puertas_ciudad_0204:
    c_peasants "All for the dance the shepherd dressed,\nIn ribbons, wreath, and gayest vest\nHimself with care arraying:\nAround the linden lass and lad"
    c_peasants "Already footed it like mad:\nHurrah! hurrah!\nHurrah—tarara-la!\nThe fiddle-bow was playing."
    c_peasants "He broke the ranks, no whit afraid,\nAnd with his elbow punched a maid,\nWho stood, the dance surveying:\nThe buxom wench, she turned and said:"
    c_peasants "“Now, you I call a stupid-head!”\nHurrah! hurrah!\nHurrah—tarara-la!\n“Be decent while you’re staying!”"
    c_peasants "Then round the circle went their flight,\nThey danced to left, they danced to right:\nTheir kirtles all were playing.\nThey first grew red, and then grew warm,"
    c_peasants "And rested, panting, arm in arm,—\nHurrah! hurrah!\nHurrah—tarara-la!\nAnd hips and elbows straying."
    c_peasants "Now, don’t be so familiar here!\nHow many a one has fooled his dear,\nWaylaying and betraying!"
    c_peasants "And yet, he coaxed her soon aside,\nAnd round the linden sounded wide.\nHurrah! hurrah!\nHurrah—tarara-la!"
    c_peasants "And the fiddle-bow was playing."

