translate english gabinete_1_0051:
    voice sustain
    c_narrator "He opens a volume, and commences."

translate english gabinete_1_0052:
    voice sustain
    c_faust "’Tis written: “In the Beginning was the Word.”\nHere am I balked: who, now can help afford?\nThe Word?—impossible so high to rate it;\nAnd otherwise must I translate it."
    voice sustain
    c_faust "If by the Spirit I am truly taught.\nThen thus: “In the Beginning was the Thought”\nThis first line let me weigh completely,\nLest my impatient pen proceed too fleetly."
    voice sustain
    c_faust "Is it the Thought which works, creates, indeed?\n“In the Beginning was the Power,” I read.\nYet, as I write, a warning is suggested,\nThat I the sense may not have fairly tested."
    voice sustain
    c_faust "The Spirit aids me: now I see the light!\n“In the Beginning was the Act,” I write."
    voice sustain
    c_faust "If I must share my chamber with thee,\nPoodle, stop that howling, prithee!\nCease to bark and bellow!\nSuch a noisy, disturbing fellow"
    voice sustain
    c_faust "I’ll no longer suffer near me.\nOne of us, dost hear me!\nMust leave, I fear me.\nNo longer guest-right I bestow;"
    voice sustain
    c_faust "The door is open, art free to go.\nBut what do I see in the creature?\nIs that in the course of nature?\nIs’t actual fact? or Fancy’s shows?"
    voice sustain
    c_faust "How long and broad my poodle grows!\nHe rises mightily:\nA canine form that cannot be!\nWhat a spectre I’ve harbored thus!"
    voice sustain
    c_faust "He resembles a hippopotamus,\nWith fiery eyes, teeth terrible to see:\nO, now am I sure of thee!\nFor all of thy half-hellish brood"
    voice sustain
    c_faust "The Key of Solomon is good."

