translate english gabinete_2_0447:
    voice sustain
    c_narrator "A STUDENT enters."

translate english gabinete_2_0448:
    voice "voice/gabinete_2_0448.ogg"
    c_student "A short time, only, am I here,\nAnd come, devoted and sincere,\nTo greet and know the man of fame,\nWhom men to me with reverence name."

translate english gabinete_2_0452:
    voice "voice/gabinete_2_0452.ogg"
    c_mephisto "Your courtesy doth flatter me:\nYou see a man, as others be.\nHave you, perchance, elsewhere begun?"

translate english gabinete_2_0455:
    voice "voice/gabinete_2_0455.ogg"
    c_student "Receive me now, I pray, as one\nWho comes to you with courage good,\nSomewhat of cash, and healthy blood:\nMy mother was hardly willing to let me;"
    voice sustain
    c_student "But knowledge worth having I fain would get me."

translate english gabinete_2_0456:
    pass

translate english gabinete_2_0460:
    pass

translate english gabinete_2_0463:
    voice "voice/gabinete_2_0463.ogg"
    c_mephisto "Then you have reached the right place now."

translate english gabinete_2_0465:
    voice "voice/gabinete_2_0465.ogg"
    c_student "I’d like to leave it, I must avow;\nI find these walls, these vaulted spaces\nAre anything but pleasant places.\nTis all so cramped and close and mean;"
    voice sustain
    c_student "One sees no tree, no glimpse of green,\nAnd when the lecture-halls receive me,\nSeeing, hearing, and thinking leave me."

translate english gabinete_2_0469:
    pass

translate english gabinete_2_0473:
    voice "voice/gabinete_2_0473.ogg"
    c_mephisto "All that depends on habitude.\nSo from its mother’s breasts a child\nAt first, reluctant, takes its food,\nBut soon to seek them is beguiled."
    voice sustain
    c_mephisto "Thus, at the breasts of Wisdom clinging,\nThou’lt find each day a greater rapture bringing."

translate english gabinete_2_0477:
    pass

translate english gabinete_2_0481:
    c_student "I’ll hang thereon with joy, and freely drain them;\nBut tell me, pray, the proper means to gain them."

translate english gabinete_2_0483:
    voice "voice/gabinete_2_0483.ogg"
    c_mephisto "Explain, before you further speak,\nThe special faculty you seek."

translate english gabinete_2_0484:
    pass

translate english gabinete_2_0486:
    voice "voice/gabinete_2_0486.ogg"
    c_student "I crave the highest erudition;\nAnd fain would make my acquisition\nAll that there is in Earth and Heaven,\nIn Nature and in Science too."

translate english gabinete_2_0490:
    voice "voice/gabinete_2_0490.ogg"
    c_mephisto "Here is the genuine path for you;\nYet strict attention must be given."

translate english gabinete_2_0493:
    voice "voice/gabinete_2_0493.ogg"
    c_student "Body and soul thereon I’ll wreak;\nYet, truly, I’ve some inclination\nOn summer holidays to seek\nA little freedom and recreation."

translate english gabinete_2_0497:
    pass

translate english gabinete_2_0498:
    voice "voice/gabinete_2_0498.ogg"
    c_mephisto "Use well your time! It flies so swiftly from us;\nBut time through order may be won, I promise.\nSo, Friend (my views to briefly sum),\nFirst, the collegium logicum."
    voice sustain
    c_mephisto "There will your mind be drilled and braced,\nAs if in Spanish boots ’twere laced,\nAnd thus, to graver paces brought,\n’Twill plod along the path of thought,"
    voice sustain
    c_mephisto "Instead of shooting here and there,\nA will-o’-the-wisp in murky air.\nDays will be spent to bid you know,\nWhat once you did at a single blow,"
    voice sustain
    c_mephisto "Like eating and drinking, free and strong,—\nThat one, two, three! thereto belong.\nTruly the fabric of mental fleece\nResembles a weaver’s masterpiece,"
    voice sustain
    c_mephisto "Where a thousand threads one treadle throws,\nWhere fly the shuttles hither and thither.\nUnseen the threads are knit together.\nAnd an infinite combination grows."
    voice sustain
    c_mephisto "Then, the philosopher steps in\nAnd shows, no otherwise it could have been:\nThe first was so, the second so,\nTherefore the third and fourth are so;"
    voice sustain
    c_mephisto "Were not the first and second, then\nThe third and fourth had never been.\nThe scholars are everywhere believers,\nBut never succeed in being weavers."
    voice sustain
    c_mephisto "He who would study organic existence,\nFirst drives out the soul with rigid persistence;\nThen the parts in his hand he may hold and class,\nBut the spiritual link is lost, alas!"
    voice sustain
    c_mephisto "Encheiresin natures, this Chemistry names,\nNor knows how herself she banters and blames!"

