translate english cocina_bruja_0001:
    c_narrator "Upon a low hearth stands a great caldron, under which a fire is burning. Various figures appear in the vapors which rise from the caldron. An ape sits beside it, skims it, and watches lest it boil over."
    c_narrator "The he-ape, with the young ones, sits near and warms himself. Ceiling and walls are covered with the most fantastic witch-implements."

translate english cocina_bruja_0003:
    voice "voice/cocina_bruja_0003.ogg"
    c_faust "These crazy signs of witches’ craft repel me!\nI shall recover, dost thou tell me,\nThrough this insane, chaotic play?\nFrom an old hag shall I demand assistance?"
    voice sustain
    c_faust "And will her foul mess take away\nFull thirty years from my existence?\nWoe’s me, canst thou naught better find!\nAnother baffled hope must be lamented:"
    voice sustain
    c_faust "Has Nature, then, and has a noble mind\nNot any potent balsam yet invented?"

translate english cocina_bruja_0007:
    pass

translate english cocina_bruja_0011:
    pass

translate english cocina_bruja_0015:
    voice "voice/cocina_bruja_0015.ogg"
    c_mephisto "Once more, my friend, thou talkest sensibly.\nThere is, to make thee young, a simpler mode and apter;\nBut in another book ’tis writ for thee,\nAnd is a most eccentric chapter."

translate english cocina_bruja_0019:
    pass

translate english cocina_bruja_0021:
    voice "voice/cocina_bruja_0021.ogg"
    c_faust "Yet will I know it."

translate english cocina_bruja_0022:
    voice "voice/cocina_bruja_0022.ogg"
    c_mephisto "Good! the method is revealed\nWithout or gold or magic or physician.\nBetake thyself to yonder field,\nThere hoe and dig, as thy condition;"
    voice sustain
    c_mephisto "Restrain thyself, thy sense and will\nWithin a narrow sphere to flourish;\nWith unmixed food thy body nourish;\nLive with the ox as ox, and think it not a theft"
    voice sustain
    c_mephisto "That thou manur’st the acre which thou reapest;—\nThat, trust me, is the best mode left,\nWhereby for eighty years thy youth thou keepest!"

translate english cocina_bruja_0023:
    pass

translate english cocina_bruja_0027:
    pass

translate english cocina_bruja_0031:
    pass

translate english cocina_bruja_0034:
    voice "voice/cocina_bruja_0034.ogg"
    c_faust "I am not used to that; I cannot stoop to try it—\nTo take the spade in hand, and ply it.\nThe narrow being suits me not at all."

translate english cocina_bruja_0038:
    voice "voice/cocina_bruja_0038.ogg"
    c_mephisto "Then to thine aid the witch must call."

translate english cocina_bruja_0039:
    voice "voice/cocina_bruja_0039.ogg"
    c_faust "Wherefore the hag, and her alone?\nCanst thou thyself not brew the potion?"

translate english cocina_bruja_0042:
    voice "voice/cocina_bruja_0042.ogg"
    c_mephisto "That were a charming sport, I own:\nI’d build a thousand bridges meanwhile, I’ve a notion.\nNot Art and Science serve, alone;\nPatience must in the work be shown."
    voice sustain
    c_mephisto "Long is the calm brain active in creation;\nTime, only, strengthens the fine fermentation.\nAnd all, belonging thereunto,\nIs rare and strange, howe’er you take it:"
    voice sustain
    c_mephisto "The Devil taught the thing, ’tis true,\nAnd yet the Devil cannot make it."

translate english cocina_bruja_0046:
    pass

translate english cocina_bruja_0050:
    pass

translate english cocina_bruja_0052:
    voice sustain
    c_narrator "Perceiving the Animals"

translate english cocina_bruja_0053:
    voice sustain
    c_mephisto "See, what a delicate race they be!\nThat is the maid! the man is he!"

translate english cocina_bruja_0055:
    voice sustain
    c_narrator "To the Animals"

translate english cocina_bruja_0056:
    voice sustain
    c_mephisto "It seems the mistress has gone away?"

translate english cocina_bruja_0057:
    voice "voice/cocina_bruja_0057.ogg"
    c_apes "Carousing, to-day!\nOff and about,\nBy the chimney out!"

translate english cocina_bruja_0060:
    voice "voice/cocina_bruja_0060.ogg"
    c_mephisto "What time takes she for dissipating?"

translate english cocina_bruja_0061:
    voice "voice/cocina_bruja_0061.ogg"
    c_apes "While we to warm our paws are waiting."

translate english cocina_bruja_0063:
    voice "voice/cocina_bruja_0063.ogg"
    c_mephisto "How findest thou the tender creatures?"

translate english cocina_bruja_0064:
    pass

translate english cocina_bruja_0065:
    c_faust "Absurder than I ever yet did see."

translate english cocina_bruja_0066:
    voice "voice/cocina_bruja_0066.ogg"
    c_mephisto "Why, just such talk as this, for me,\nIs that which has the most attractive features!"

translate english cocina_bruja_0068:
    voice sustain
    c_narrator "To the Animals"

translate english cocina_bruja_0069:
    voice sustain
    c_mephisto "But tell me now, ye cursed puppets,\nWhy do ye stir the porridge so?"

translate english cocina_bruja_0071:
    voice "voice/cocina_bruja_0071.ogg"
    c_apes "We’re cooking watery soup for beggars."

translate english cocina_bruja_0072:
    voice "voice/cocina_bruja_0072.ogg"
    c_mephisto "Then a great public you can show."
    voice sustain
    c_narrator "THE HE-APE (comes up and fawns on MEPHISTOPHELES)"

translate english cocina_bruja_0073:
    voice "voice/cocina_bruja_0073.ogg"
    c_apes "O cast thou the dice!\nMake me rich in a trice,\nLet me win in good season!\nThings are badly controlled,"
    voice sustain
    c_apes "And had I but gold,\nSo had I my reason."

translate english cocina_bruja_0077:
    pass

translate english cocina_bruja_0080:
    voice "voice/cocina_bruja_0080.ogg"
    c_mephisto "How would the ape be sure his luck enhances.\nCould he but try the lottery’s chances!"

translate english cocina_bruja_0082:
    voice sustain
    c_narrator "In the meantime the young apes have been playing with a large ball, which they now roll forward."

translate english cocina_bruja_0083:
    voice "voice/cocina_bruja_0083.ogg"
    c_apes "The world’s the ball:\nDoth rise and fall,\nAnd roll incessant:\nLike glass doth ring,"
    voice sustain
    c_apes "A hollow thing,—\nHow soon will’t spring,\nAnd drop, quiescent?\nHere bright it gleams,"
    voice sustain
    c_apes "Here brighter seems:\nI live at present!\nDear son, I say,\nKeep thou away!"
    voice sustain
    c_apes "Thy doom is spoken!\n’Tis made of clay,\nAnd will be broken."

translate english cocina_bruja_0087:
    pass

translate english cocina_bruja_0091:
    pass

translate english cocina_bruja_0095:
    voice "voice/cocina_bruja_0095.ogg"
    c_mephisto "What means the sieve?"

translate english cocina_bruja_0096:
    voice "voice/cocina_bruja_0096.ogg"
    c_apes "Wert thou the thief,\nI’d know him and shame him."

translate english cocina_bruja_0099:
    voice sustain
    c_narrator "He runs to the SHE-APE, and lets her look through it."

translate english cocina_bruja_0100:
    voice sustain
    c_apes "Look through the sieve!\nKnow’st thou the thief,\nAnd darest not name him?"

translate english cocina_bruja_0103:
    voice "voice/cocina_bruja_0103.ogg"
    c_mephisto "And what’s this pot?"

translate english cocina_bruja_0104:
    voice "voice/cocina_bruja_0104.ogg"
    c_apes "The fool knows it not!\nHe knows not the pot,\nHe knows not the kettle!"

translate english cocina_bruja_0107:
    c_mephisto "Impertinent beast!"

translate english cocina_bruja_0110:
    voice "voice/cocina_bruja_0110.ogg"
    c_apes "Take the brush here, at least,\nAnd sit down on the settle!"

translate english cocina_bruja_0114:
    voice sustain
    c_narrator "He invites MEPHISTOPHELES to sit down."

translate english cocina_bruja_0115:
    c_narrator "FAUST (who during all this time has been standing before a mirror, now approaching and now retreating from it)"

translate english cocina_bruja_0116:
    voice "voice/cocina_bruja_0116.ogg"
    c_faust "What do I see? What heavenly form revealed\nShows through the glass from Magic’s fair dominions!\nO lend me, Love, the swiftest of thy pinions,\nAnd bear me to her beauteous field!"
    voice sustain
    c_faust "Ah, if I leave this spot with fond designing,\nIf I attempt to venture near,\nDim, as through gathering mist, her charms appear!—\nA woman’s form, in beauty shining!"
    voice sustain
    c_faust "Can woman, then, so lovely be?\nAnd must I find her body, there reclining,\nOf all the heavens the bright epitome?\nCan Earth with such a thing be mated?"

translate english cocina_bruja_0120:
    pass

translate english cocina_bruja_0124:
    pass

translate english cocina_bruja_0128:
    pass

translate english cocina_bruja_0132:
    c_mephisto "Why, surely, if a God first plagues Himself six days,\nThen, self-contented, Bravo! says,\nMust something clever be created.\nThis time, thine eyes be satiate!"
    c_mephisto "I’ll yet detect thy sweetheart and ensnare her,\nAnd blest is he, who has the lucky fate,\nSome day, as bridegroom, home to bear her."

translate english cocina_bruja_0136:
    pass

translate english cocina_bruja_0140:
    pass

translate english cocina_bruja_0144:
    c_narrator "FAUST gazes continually in the mirror. MEPHISTOPHELES, stretching himself out on the settle, and playing with the brush, continues to speak."

translate english cocina_bruja_0145:
    c_mephisto "So sit I, like the King upon his throne:\nI hold the sceptre, here,—and lack the crown alone."

translate english cocina_bruja_0149:
    c_narrator "THE ANIMALS (who up to this time have been making all kinds of fantastic movements together bring a crown to MEPHISTOPHELES with great noise.)"

translate english cocina_bruja_0150:
    c_apes "O be thou so good\nWith sweat and with blood\nThe crown to belime!"

translate english cocina_bruja_0152:
    c_narrator "They handle the crown awkwardly and break it into two pieces, with which they spring around."

translate english cocina_bruja_0153:
    c_apes "’Tis done, let it be!\nWe speak and we see,\nWe hear and we rhyme!"

translate english cocina_bruja_0155:
    voice "voice/cocina_bruja_0155.ogg"
    c_faust "Woe’s me! I fear to lose my wits."

translate english cocina_bruja_0157:
    voice "voice/cocina_bruja_0157.ogg"
    c_mephisto "My own head, now, is really nigh to sinking."

translate english cocina_bruja_0159:
    voice "voice/cocina_bruja_0159.ogg"
    c_apes "If lucky our hits,\nAnd everything fits,\n’Tis thoughts, and we’re thinking!"

translate english cocina_bruja_0161:
    c_faust "My bosom burns with that sweet vision;\nLet us, with speed, away from here!"

translate english cocina_bruja_0162:
    voice "voice/cocina_bruja_0162.ogg"
    c_mephisto "One must, at least, make this admission—\nThey’re poets, genuine and sincere."

translate english cocina_bruja_0165:
    voice sustain
    c_narrator "The caldron, which the SHE-APE has up to this time neglected to watch, begins to boil over: there ensues a great flame, which blazes out the chimney. The WITCH comes careering down through the flame, with terrible cries."

translate english cocina_bruja_0166:
    voice "voice/cocina_bruja_0166.ogg"
    c_witch "Ow! ow! ow! ow!\nThe damnéd beast—the curséd sow!\nTo leave the kettle, and singe the Frau!\nAccurséd fere!"

translate english cocina_bruja_0170:
    pass

translate english cocina_bruja_0171:
    pass

translate english cocina_bruja_0172:
    pass

translate english cocina_bruja_0173:
    voice sustain
    c_narrator "Perceiving FAUST and MEPHISTOPHELES."

translate english cocina_bruja_0174:
    voice sustain
    c_witch "What is that here?\nWho are you here?\nWhat want you thus?\nWho sneaks to us?"
    voice sustain
    c_witch "The fire-pain\nBurn bone and brain!"

translate english cocina_bruja_0178:
    pass

translate english cocina_bruja_0179:
    pass

translate english cocina_bruja_0181:
    voice sustain
    c_narrator "She plunges the skimming-ladle into the caldron, and scatters flames towards FAUST, MEPHISTOPHELES, and the Animals. The Animals whimper."

translate english cocina_bruja_0182:
    c_narrator "MEPHISTOPHELES (reversing the brush, which he has been holding in his hand, and striding among the jars and glasses)"

translate english cocina_bruja_0183:
    voice "voice/cocina_bruja_0183.ogg"
    c_mephisto "In two! in two!\nThere lies the brew!\nThere lies the glass!\nThe joke will pass,"
    voice sustain
    c_mephisto "As time, foul ass!\nTo the singing of thy crew."

translate english cocina_bruja_0187:
    pass

translate english cocina_bruja_0188:
    pass

translate english cocina_bruja_0190:
    voice sustain
    c_narrator "As the WITCH starts back, full of wrath and horror"

translate english cocina_bruja_0191:
    voice sustain
    c_mephisto "Ha! know’st thou me? Abomination, thou!\nKnow’st thou, at last, thy Lord and Master?\nWhat hinders me from smiting now\nThee and thy monkey-sprites with fell disaster?"
    voice sustain
    c_mephisto "Hast for the scarlet coat no reverence?\nDost recognize no more the tall cock’s-feather?\nHave I concealed this countenance?—\nMust tell my name, old face of leather?"

translate english cocina_bruja_0195:
    pass

translate english cocina_bruja_0199:
    pass

translate english cocina_bruja_0203:
    voice "voice/cocina_bruja_0203.ogg"
    c_witch "O pardon, Sir, the rough salute!\nYet I perceive no cloven foot;\nAnd both your ravens, where are they now?"

translate english cocina_bruja_0207:
    voice "voice/cocina_bruja_0207.ogg"
    c_mephisto "This time, I’ll let thee ’scape the debt;\nFor since we two together met,\n’Tis verily full many a day now.\nCulture, which smooth the whole world licks,"
    voice sustain
    c_mephisto "Also unto the Devil sticks.\nThe days of that old Northern phantom now are over:\nWhere canst thou horns and tail and claws discover?\nAnd, as regards the foot, which I can’t spare, in truth,"
    voice sustain
    c_mephisto "’Twould only make the people shun me;\nTherefore I’ve worn, like many a spindly youth,\nFalse calves these many years upon me."

translate english cocina_bruja_0208:
    pass

translate english cocina_bruja_0212:
    pass

translate english cocina_bruja_0216:
    pass

translate english cocina_bruja_0220:
    pass

translate english cocina_bruja_0222:
    voice "voice/cocina_bruja_0222.ogg"
    c_witch "Reason and sense forsake my brain,\nSince I behold Squire Satan here again!"

translate english cocina_bruja_0224:
    c_mephisto "Woman, from such a name refrain!"

translate english cocina_bruja_0226:
    voice "voice/cocina_bruja_0226.ogg"
    c_witch "Why so? What has it done to thee?"

translate english cocina_bruja_0227:
    voice "voice/cocina_bruja_0227.ogg"
    c_mephisto "It’s long been written in the Book of Fable;\nYet, therefore, no whit better men we see:\nThe Evil One has left, the evil ones are stable.\nSir Baron call me thou, then is the matter good;"
    voice sustain
    c_mephisto "A cavalier am I, like others in my bearing.\nThou hast no doubt about my noble blood:\nSee, here’s the coat-of-arms that I am wearing!"

translate english cocina_bruja_0228:
    pass

translate english cocina_bruja_0232:
    pass

translate english cocina_bruja_0236:
    pass

translate english cocina_bruja_0237:
    voice sustain
    c_narrator "He makes an indecent gesture."

translate english cocina_bruja_0238:
    voice "voice/cocina_bruja_0238.ogg"
    c_witch "Ha! ha! That’s just your way, I know:\nA rogue you are, and you were always so."

translate english cocina_bruja_0240:
    voice "voice/cocina_bruja_0240.ogg"
    c_mephisto "My friend, take proper heed, I pray!\nTo manage witches, this is just the way."

translate english cocina_bruja_0242:
    voice "voice/cocina_bruja_0242.ogg"
    c_witch "Wherein, Sirs, can I be of use?"

translate english cocina_bruja_0243:
    pass

translate english cocina_bruja_0244:
    voice "voice/cocina_bruja_0244.ogg"
    c_mephisto "Give us a goblet of the well-known juice!\nBut, I must beg you, of the oldest brewage;\nThe years a double strength produce."

translate english cocina_bruja_0245:
    pass

translate english cocina_bruja_0248:
    voice "voice/cocina_bruja_0248.ogg"
    c_witch "With all my heart! Now, here’s a bottle,\nWherefrom, sometimes, I wet my throttle,\nWhich, also, not the slightest, stinks;\nAnd willingly a glass I’ll fill him."

translate english cocina_bruja_0249:
    pass

translate english cocina_bruja_0253:
    voice sustain
    c_narrator "Whispering"

translate english cocina_bruja_0254:
    voice sustain
    c_witch "Yet, if this man without due preparation drinks,\nAs well thou know’st, within an hour ’twill kill him."

translate english cocina_bruja_0257:
    voice "voice/cocina_bruja_0257.ogg"
    c_mephisto "He is a friend of mine, with whom it will agree,\nAnd he deserves thy kitchen’s best potation:\nCome, draw thy circle, speak thine adjuration,\nAnd fill thy goblet full and free!"

translate english cocina_bruja_0261:
    pass

translate english cocina_bruja_0264:
    voice sustain
    c_narrator "THE WITCH (with fantastic gestures draws a circle and places mysterious articles therein; meanwhile the glasses begin to ring, the caldron to sound, and make a musical accompaniment."
    voice sustain
    c_narrator "Finally she brings a great book, and stations in the circle the Apes, who are obliged to serve as reading-desk, and to hold the torches. She then beckons FAUST to approach.)"

translate english cocina_bruja_0265:
    voice "voice/cocina_bruja_0265.ogg"
    c_faust "Now, what shall come of this? the creatures antic,\nThe crazy stuff, the gestures frantic,—\nAll the repulsive cheats I view,—\nAre known to me, and hated, too."

translate english cocina_bruja_0269:
    voice "voice/cocina_bruja_0269.ogg"
    c_mephisto "O, nonsense! That’s a thing for laughter;\nDon’t be so terribly severe!\nShe juggles you as doctor now, that, after,\nThe beverage may work the proper cheer."

translate english cocina_bruja_0273:
    pass

translate english cocina_bruja_0275:
    voice sustain
    c_narrator "He persuades FAUST to step into the circle."

translate english cocina_bruja_0276:
    c_narrator "THE WITCH (begins to declaim, with much emphasis, from the book)"

translate english cocina_bruja_0277:
    voice "voice/cocina_bruja_0277.ogg"
    c_witch "See, thus it’s done!\nMake ten of one,\nAnd two let be,\nMake even three,"
    voice sustain
    c_witch "And rich thou ’It be.\nCast o’er the four!\nFrom five and six\n(The witch’s tricks)"
    voice sustain
    c_witch "Make seven and eight,\n’Tis finished straight!\nAnd nine is one,\nAnd ten is none."
    voice sustain
    c_witch "This is the witch’s once-one’s-one!"

translate english cocina_bruja_0281:
    pass

translate english cocina_bruja_0282:
    pass

translate english cocina_bruja_0283:
    pass

translate english cocina_bruja_0284:
    pass

translate english cocina_bruja_0285:
    pass

translate english cocina_bruja_0289:
    pass

translate english cocina_bruja_0292:
    c_faust "She talks like one who raves in fever."

translate english cocina_bruja_0294:
    voice "voice/cocina_bruja_0294.ogg"
    c_mephisto "Thou’lt hear much more before we leave her.\n’Tis all the same: the book I can repeat,\nSuch time I’ve squandered o’er the history:\nA contradiction thus complete"
    voice sustain
    c_mephisto "Is always for the wise, no less than fools, a mystery.\nThe art is old and new, for verily\nAll ages have been taught the matter,—\nBy Three and One, and One and Three,"
    voice sustain
    c_mephisto "Error instead of Truth to scatter.\nThey prate and teach, and no one interferes;\nAll from the fellowship of fools are shrinking.\nMan usually believes, if only words he hears,"
    voice sustain
    c_mephisto "That also with them goes material for thinking!"

translate english cocina_bruja_0295:
    pass

translate english cocina_bruja_0299:
    pass

translate english cocina_bruja_0303:
    pass

translate english cocina_bruja_0307:
    pass

translate english cocina_bruja_0311:
    pass

translate english cocina_bruja_0313:
    voice "voice/cocina_bruja_0313.ogg"
    c_witch "The lofty skill\nOf Science, still\nFrom all men deeply hidden!\nWho takes no thought,"
    voice sustain
    c_witch "To him ’tis brought,\n’Tis given unsought, unbidden!"

translate english cocina_bruja_0317:
    pass

translate english cocina_bruja_0318:
    pass

translate english cocina_bruja_0320:
    voice "voice/cocina_bruja_0320.ogg"
    c_faust "What nonsense she declaims before us!\nMy head is nigh to split, I fear:\nIt seems to me as if I hear\nA hundred thousand fools in chorus."

translate english cocina_bruja_0324:
    c_mephisto "O Sibyl excellent, enough of adjuration!\nBut hither bring us thy potation,\nAnd quickly fill the beaker to the brim!\nThis drink will bring my friend no injuries:"
    c_mephisto "He is a man of manifold degrees,\nAnd many draughts are known to him."

translate english cocina_bruja_0328:
    pass

translate english cocina_bruja_0330:
    c_narrator "The WITCH, with many ceremonies, pours the drink into a cup; as FAUST sets it to his lips, a light flame arises."

translate english cocina_bruja_0331:
    c_mephisto "Down with it quickly! Drain it off!\n’Twill warm thy heart with new desire:\nArt with the Devil hand and glove,\nAnd wilt thou be afraid of fire?"

translate english cocina_bruja_0335:
    c_narrator "The WITCH breaks the circle: FAUST steps forth."

translate english cocina_bruja_0336:
    c_mephisto "And now, away! Thou dar’st not rest."

translate english cocina_bruja_0337:
    voice "voice/cocina_bruja_0337.ogg"
    c_witch "And much good may the liquor do thee!"

translate english cocina_bruja_0338:
    voice "voice/cocina_bruja_0338.ogg"
    c_mephisto "Thy wish be on Walpurgis Night expressed;\nWhat boon I have, shall then be given unto thee."

translate english cocina_bruja_0341:
    voice "voice/cocina_bruja_0341.ogg"
    c_witch "Here is a song, which, if you sometimes sing,\nYou’ll find it of peculiar operation."

translate english cocina_bruja_0345:
    voice "voice/cocina_bruja_0345.ogg"
    c_mephisto "Come, walk at once! A rapid occupation\nMust start the needful perspiration,\nAnd through thy frame the liquor’s potence fling.\nThe noble indolence I’ll teach thee then to treasure,"
    voice sustain
    c_mephisto "And soon thou’lt be aware, with keenest thrills of pleasure,\nHow Cupid stirs and leaps, on light and restless wing."

translate english cocina_bruja_0349:
    pass

translate english cocina_bruja_0353:
    pass

translate english cocina_bruja_0355:
    voice "voice/cocina_bruja_0355.ogg"
    c_faust "One rapid glance within the mirror give me,\nHow beautiful that woman-form!"

translate english cocina_bruja_0359:
    voice "voice/cocina_bruja_0359.ogg"
    c_mephisto "No, no! The paragon of all, believe me,\nThou soon shalt see, alive and warm."

translate english cocina_bruja_0363:
    voice sustain
    c_narrator "Aside"

translate english cocina_bruja_0364:
    voice sustain
    c_mephisto "Thou’lt find, this drink thy blood compelling,\nEach woman beautiful as Helen!"

translate english calle_1_0002:
    voice "voice/calle_1_0002.ogg"
    c_faust "Fair lady, let it not offend you,\nThat arm and escort I would lend you!"

translate english calle_1_0004:
    voice "voice/calle_1_0004.ogg"
    c_margarita "I’m neither lady, neither fair,\nAnd home I can go without your care."

translate english calle_1_0006:
    voice sustain
    c_narrator "She releases herself, and exit."

translate english calle_1_0007:
    voice "voice/calle_1_0007.ogg"
    c_faust "By Heaven, the girl is wondrous fair!\nOf all I’ve seen, beyond compare;\nSo sweetly virtuous and pure,\nAnd yet a little pert, be sure!"
    voice sustain
    c_faust "The lip so red, the cheek’s clear dawn,\nI’ll not forget while the world rolls on!\nHow she cast down her timid eyes,\nDeep in my heart imprinted lies:"
    voice sustain
    c_faust "How short and sharp of speech was she,\nWhy, ’twas a real ecstasy!"

translate english calle_1_0011:
    pass

translate english calle_1_0015:
    pass

translate english calle_1_0019:
    pass

translate english calle_1_0023:
    voice sustain
    c_narrator "MEPHISTOPHELES enters"

translate english calle_1_0024:
    voice "voice/calle_1_0024.ogg"
    c_faust "Hear, of that girl I’d have possession!"

translate english calle_1_0026:
    voice "voice/calle_1_0026.ogg"
