translate english cuartito_0027:
    voice sustain
    c_narrator "He throws himself into a leathern arm-chair near the bed."

translate english cuartito_0028:
    voice sustain
    c_faust "Receive me, thou, that in thine open arms\nDeparted joy and pain wert wont to gather!\nHow oft the children, with their ruddy charms,\nHung here, around this throne, where sat the father!"
    voice sustain
    c_faust "Perchance my love, amid the childish band,\nGrateful for gifts the Holy Christmas gave her,\nHere meekly kissed the grandsire’s withered hand.\nI feel, O maid! thy very soul"
    voice sustain
    c_faust "Of order and content around me whisper,—\nWhich leads thee with its motherly control,\nThe cloth upon thy board bids smoothly thee unroll,\nThe sand beneath thy feet makes whiter, crisper."
    voice sustain
    c_faust "O dearest hand, to thee ’tis given\nTo change this hut into a lower heaven!\nAnd here!"

