    nvl clear
    voice sustain
    c_margarita_nvl "Naught was to him more precious;\nHe drained it at every bout:\nHis eyes with tears ran over,\nAs oft as he drank thereout."
    nvl clear
    voice sustain
    c_margarita_nvl "When came his time of dying,\nThe towns in his land he told,\nNaught else to his heir denying\nExcept the goblet of gold."
    nvl clear
    voice sustain
    c_margarita_nvl "He sat at the royal banquet\nWith his knights of high degree,\nIn the lofty hall of his fathers\nIn the Castle by the Sea."
    nvl clear
    voice sustain
    c_margarita_nvl "There stood the old carouser,\nAnd drank the last life-glow;\nAnd hurled the hallowed goblet\nInto the tide below."
    nvl clear
    voice sustain
    c_margarita_nvl "He saw it plunging and filling,\nAnd sinking deep in the sea:\nThen fell his eyelids forever,\nAnd never more drank he!"

