translate english casa_vecina_0091:
    voice "voice/casa_vecina_0091.ogg"
    c_mephisto "In Padua buried, he is lying\nBeside the good Saint Antony,\nWithin a grave well consecrated,\nFor cool, eternal rest created."

translate english casa_vecina_0095:
    voice "voice/casa_vecina_0095.ogg"
    c_marta "He gave you, further, no commission?"

translate english casa_vecina_0096:
    voice "voice/casa_vecina_0096.ogg"
    c_mephisto "Yes, one of weight, with many sighs:\nThree hundred masses buy, to save him from perdition!\nMy hands are empty, otherwise."

translate english casa_vecina_0097:
    pass

translate english casa_vecina_0101:
    voice "voice/casa_vecina_0101.ogg"
    c_marta "What! Not a pocket-piece? no jewelry?\nWhat every journeyman within his wallet spares,\nAnd as a token with him bears,\nAnd rather starves or begs, than loses?"

translate english casa_vecina_0105:
    pass

translate english casa_vecina_0108:
    voice "voice/casa_vecina_0108.ogg"
    c_mephisto "Madam, it is a grief to me;\nYet, on my word, his cash was put to proper uses.\nBesides, his penitence was very sore,\nAnd he lamented his ill fortune all the more."

translate english casa_vecina_0112:
    pass

translate english casa_vecina_0114:
    voice "voice/casa_vecina_0114.ogg"
    c_margarita "Alack, that men are so unfortunate!\nSurely for his soul’s sake full many a prayer I’ll proffer."

translate english casa_vecina_0116:
    voice "voice/casa_vecina_0116.ogg"
    c_mephisto "You well deserve a speedy marriage-offer:\nYou are so kind, compassionate."

translate english casa_vecina_0117:
    pass

translate english casa_vecina_0119:
    c_margarita "O, no! As yet, it would not do."

translate english casa_vecina_0120:
    voice "voice/casa_vecina_0120.ogg"
    c_mephisto "If not a husband, then a beau for you!\nIt is the greatest heavenly blessing,\nTo have a dear thing for one’s caressing."

translate english casa_vecina_0121:
    pass

translate english casa_vecina_0124:
    voice "voice/casa_vecina_0124.ogg"
    c_margarita "The country’s custom is not so."

translate english casa_vecina_0126:
    voice "voice/casa_vecina_0126.ogg"
    c_mephisto "Custom, or not! It happens, though."

translate english casa_vecina_0127:
    pass

translate english casa_vecina_0128:
    voice "voice/casa_vecina_0128.ogg"
    c_marta "Continue, pray!"

translate english casa_vecina_0129:
    pass

translate english casa_vecina_0130:
    voice "voice/casa_vecina_0130.ogg"
    c_mephisto "I stood beside his bed of dying.\n’Twas something better than manure,—\nHalf-rotten straw: and yet, he died a Christian, sure,\nAnd found that heavier scores to his account were lying."
    voice sustain
    c_mephisto "He cried: “I find my conduct wholly hateful!\nTo leave my wife, my trade, in manner so ungrateful!\nAh, the remembrance makes me die!\nWould of my wrong to her I might be shriven!”"

translate english casa_vecina_0134:
    pass

translate english casa_vecina_0138:
    pass

translate english casa_vecina_0142:
    c_marta "The dear, good man! Long since was he forgiven."

translate english casa_vecina_0143:
    voice "voice/casa_vecina_0143.ogg"
    c_mephisto "“Yet she, God knows! was more to blame than I.”"

translate english casa_vecina_0144:
    pass

translate english casa_vecina_0146:
    voice "voice/casa_vecina_0146.ogg"
    c_marta "He lied! What! On the brink of death he slandered?"

translate english casa_vecina_0147:
    pass

translate english casa_vecina_0149:
    voice "voice/casa_vecina_0149.ogg"
    c_mephisto "In the last throes his senses wandered,\nIf I such things but half can judge.\nHe said: “I had no time for play, for gaping freedom:\nFirst children, and then work for bread to feed ’em,—"
    voice sustain
    c_mephisto "For bread, in the widest sense, to drudge,\nAnd could not even eat my share in peace and quiet!”"

translate english casa_vecina_0150:
    pass

translate english casa_vecina_0154:
    pass

translate english casa_vecina_0158:
    pass

translate english casa_vecina_0159:
    voice "voice/casa_vecina_0159.ogg"
    c_marta "Had he all love, all faith forgotten in his riot?\nMy work and worry, day and night?"

translate english casa_vecina_0160:
    pass

translate english casa_vecina_0162:
    voice "voice/casa_vecina_0162.ogg"
    c_mephisto "Not so: the memory of it touched him quite.\nSaid he: “When I from Malta went away\nMy prayers for wife and little ones were zealous,\nAnd such a luck from Heaven befell us,"
    voice sustain
    c_mephisto "We made a Turkish merchantman our prey,\nThat to the Soldan bore a mighty treasure.\nThen I received, as was most fit,\nSince bravery was paid in fullest measure,"
    voice sustain
    c_mephisto "My well-apportioned share of it.”"

translate english casa_vecina_0166:
    pass

translate english casa_vecina_0170:
    pass

translate english casa_vecina_0174:
    voice "voice/casa_vecina_0174.ogg"
    c_marta "Say, how? Say, where? If buried, did he own it?"

translate english casa_vecina_0176:
    voice "voice/casa_vecina_0176.ogg"
    c_mephisto "Who knows, now, whither the four winds have blown it?\nA fair young damsel took him in her care,\nAs he in Naples wandered round, unfriended;\nAnd she much love, much faith to him did bear,"
    voice sustain
    c_mephisto "So that he felt it till his days were ended."

translate english casa_vecina_0180:
    pass

translate english casa_vecina_0184:
    voice "voice/casa_vecina_0184.ogg"
    c_marta "The villain! From his children thieving!\nEven all the misery on him cast\nCould not prevent his shameful way of living!"

translate english casa_vecina_0188:
    voice "voice/casa_vecina_0188.ogg"
    c_mephisto "But see! He’s dead therefrom, at last.\nWere I in your place, do not doubt me,\nI’d mourn him decently a year,\nAnd for another keep, meanwhile, my eyes about me."

translate english casa_vecina_0192:
    voice "voice/casa_vecina_0192.ogg"
    c_marta "Ah, God! another one so dear\nAs was my first, this world will hardly give me.\nThere never was a sweeter fool than mine,\nOnly he loved to roam and leave me,"
    voice sustain
    c_marta "And foreign wenches and foreign wine,\nAnd the damned throw of dice, indeed."

translate english casa_vecina_0196:
    pass

translate english casa_vecina_0198:
    voice "voice/casa_vecina_0198.ogg"
    c_mephisto "Well, well! That might have done, however,\nIf he had only been as clever,\nAnd treated your slips with as little heed.\nI swear, with this condition, too,"
    voice sustain
    c_mephisto "I would, myself, change rings with you."

translate english casa_vecina_0202:
    pass

translate english casa_vecina_0203:
    voice "voice/casa_vecina_0203.ogg"
    c_marta "The gentleman is pleased to jest."

translate english casa_vecina_0204:
    pass

translate english casa_vecina_0205:
    voice "voice/casa_vecina_0205.ogg"
    c_mephisto "I’ll cut away, betimes, from here:\nShe’d take the Devil at his word, I fear."

translate english casa_vecina_0208:
    voice sustain
    c_narrator "To MARGARET"

translate english casa_vecina_0209:
    voice sustain
    c_mephisto "How fares the heart within your breast?"

translate english casa_vecina_0210:
    pass

translate english casa_vecina_0211:
    voice "voice/casa_vecina_0211.ogg"
    c_margarita "What means the gentleman?"
    c_mephisto "Sweet innocent, thou art!"

translate english casa_vecina_0212:
    c_narrator "Aloud."
    c_mephisto "Ladies, farewell!"

translate english casa_vecina_0213:
    voice "voice/casa_vecina_0213.ogg"
    c_margarita "Farewell!"

translate english casa_vecina_0214:
    voice "voice/casa_vecina_0214.ogg"
    c_marta "A moment, ere we part!\nI’d like to have a legal witness,\nWhere, how, and when he died, to certify his fitness.\nIrregular ways I’ve always hated;"
    voice sustain
    c_marta "I want his death in the weekly paper stated."

translate english casa_vecina_0218:
    pass

translate english casa_vecina_0222:
    voice "voice/casa_vecina_0222.ogg"
    c_mephisto "Yes, my good dame, a pair of witnesses\nAlways the truth establishes.\nI have a friend of high condition,\nWho’ll also add his deposition."
    voice sustain
    c_mephisto "I’ll bring him here."

translate english casa_vecina_0223:
    pass

translate english casa_vecina_0227:
    pass

translate english casa_vecina_0229:
    voice "voice/casa_vecina_0229.ogg"
    c_marta "Good Sir, pray do!"

translate english casa_vecina_0230:
    voice "voice/casa_vecina_0230.ogg"
    c_mephisto "And this young lady will be present, too?\nA gallant youth! has travelled far:\nLadies with him delighted are."

translate english casa_vecina_0234:
    voice "voice/casa_vecina_0234.ogg"
    c_margarita "Before him I should blush, ashamed."

translate english casa_vecina_0235:
    pass

translate english casa_vecina_0236:
    voice "voice/casa_vecina_0236.ogg"
    c_mephisto "Before no king that could be named!"

translate english casa_vecina_0237:
    pass

translate english casa_vecina_0238:
    voice "voice/casa_vecina_0238.ogg"
    c_marta "Behind the house, in my garden, then,\nThis eve we’ll expect the gentlemen."

translate english casa_vecina_0241:
    pass

translate english calle_2_0002:
    voice "voice/calle_2_0002.ogg"
    c_faust "How is it? under way? and soon complete?"

translate english calle_2_0003:
    voice "voice/calle_2_0003.ogg"
    c_mephisto "Ah, bravo! Do I find you burning?\nWell, Margaret soon will still your yearning:\nAt Neighbor Martha’s you’ll this evening meet.\nA fitter woman ne’er was made"
    voice sustain
    c_mephisto "To ply the pimp and gypsy trade!"

translate english calle_2_0007:
    pass

translate english calle_2_0010:
    voice "voice/calle_2_0010.ogg"
    c_faust "Tis well."

translate english calle_2_0011:
    voice "voice/calle_2_0011.ogg"
    c_mephisto "Yet something is required from us."

translate english calle_2_0012:
    pass

translate english calle_2_0013:
    voice "voice/calle_2_0013.ogg"
    c_faust "One service pays the other thus."

translate english calle_2_0014:
    voice "voice/calle_2_0014.ogg"
    c_mephisto "We’ve but to make a deposition valid\nThat now her husband’s limbs, outstretched and pallid,\nAt Padua rest, in consecrated soil."

translate english calle_2_0018:
    pass

translate english calle_2_0019:
    voice "voice/calle_2_0019.ogg"
    c_faust "Most wise! And first, of course, we’ll make the journey\nthither?"

translate english calle_2_0020:
    voice "voice/calle_2_0020.ogg"
    c_mephisto "Sancta simplicitas! no need of such a toil;\nDepose, with knowledge or without it, either!"

translate english calle_2_0023:
    voice "voice/calle_2_0023.ogg"
    c_faust "If you’ve naught better, then, I’ll tear your pretty plan!"

translate english calle_2_0025:
    voice "voice/calle_2_0025.ogg"
    c_mephisto "Now, there you are! O holy man!\nIs it the first time in your life you’re driven\nTo bear false witness in a case?\nOf God, the world and all that in it has a place,"
    voice sustain
    c_mephisto "Of Man, and all that moves the being of his race,\nHave you not terms and definitions given\nWith brazen forehead, daring breast?\nAnd, if you’ll probe the thing profoundly,"
    voice sustain
    c_mephisto "Knew you so much—and you’ll confess it roundly!—\nAs here of Schwerdtlein’s death and place of rest?"

translate english calle_2_0029:
    pass

translate english calle_2_0033:
    pass

translate english calle_2_0037:
    pass

translate english calle_2_0039:
    voice "voice/calle_2_0039.ogg"
    c_faust "Thou art, and thou remain’st, a sophist, liar."

translate english calle_2_0040:
    voice "voice/calle_2_0040.ogg"
    c_mephisto "Yes, knew I not more deeply thy desire.\nFor wilt thou not, no lover fairer,\nPoor Margaret flatter, and ensnare her,\nAnd all thy soul’s devotion swear her?"

translate english calle_2_0044:
    pass

translate english calle_2_0046:
    voice "voice/calle_2_0046.ogg"
    c_faust "And from my heart."

translate english calle_2_0047:
    voice "voice/calle_2_0047.ogg"
    c_mephisto "’Tis very fine!\nThine endless love, thy faith assuring,\nThe one almighty force enduring,—\nWill that, too, prompt this heart of thine?"

translate english calle_2_0048:
    pass

translate english calle_2_0052:
    pass

translate english calle_2_0053:
    voice "voice/calle_2_0053.ogg"
    c_faust "Hold! hold! It will!—If such my flame,\nAnd for the sense and power intense\nI seek, and cannot find, a name;\nThen range with all my senses through creation,"
    voice sustain
    c_faust "Craving the speech of inspiration,\nAnd call this ardor, so supernal,\nEndless, eternal and eternal,—\nIs that a devilish lying game?"

translate english calle_2_0057:
    pass

