translate english jardin_0002:
    c_narrator "MARGARET on FAUST’S arm. MARTHA and MEPHISTOPHELES walking up and down."
    c_margarita "I feel, the gentleman allows for me,\nDemeans himself, and shames me by it;\nA traveller is so used to be\nKindly content with any diet."
    c_margarita "I know too well that my poor gossip can\nNe’er entertain such an experienced man."

translate english jardin_0006:
    pass

translate english jardin_0010:
    c_faust "A look from thee, a word, more entertains\nThan all the lore of wisest brains."

translate english jardin_0014:
    c_narrator "He kisses her hand."

translate english jardin_0015:
    voice "voice/jardin_0015.ogg"
    c_margarita "Don’t incommode yourself! How could you ever kiss it!\nIt is so ugly, rough to see!\nWhat work I do,—how hard and steady is it!\nMother is much too close with me."

translate english jardin_0019:
    pass

translate english jardin_0021:
    voice sustain
    c_narrator "They pass."

translate english jardin_0022:
    voice "voice/jardin_0022.ogg"
    c_marta "And you, Sir, travel always, do you not?"

translate english jardin_0023:
    pass

translate english jardin_0024:
    voice "voice/jardin_0024.ogg"
    c_mephisto "Alas, that trade and duty us so harry!\nWith what a pang one leaves so many a spot,\nAnd dares not even now and then to tarry!"

translate english jardin_0025:
    pass

translate english jardin_0029:
    pass

translate english jardin_0031:
    voice "voice/jardin_0031.ogg"
    c_marta "In young, wild years it suits your ways,\nThis round and round the world in freedom sweeping;\nBut then come on the evil days,\nAnd so, as bachelor, into his grave a-creeping,"
    voice sustain
    c_marta "None ever found a thing to praise."

translate english jardin_0032:
    pass

translate english jardin_0036:
    pass

translate english jardin_0039:
    voice "voice/jardin_0039.ogg"
    c_mephisto "I dread to see how such a fate advances."

translate english jardin_0041:
    voice "voice/jardin_0041.ogg"
    c_marta "Then, worthy Sir, improve betimes your chances!"

translate english jardin_0043:
    voice sustain
    c_narrator "They pass."

translate english jardin_0044:
    voice "voice/jardin_0044.ogg"
    c_margarita "Yes, out of sight is out of mind!\nYour courtesy an easy grace is;\nBut you have friends in other places,\nAnd sensibler than I, you’ll find."
    c_faust "Trust me, dear heart! what men call sensible\nIs oft mere vanity and narrowness."
    c_margarita "How so?"

translate english jardin_0048:
    voice "voice/jardin_0048.ogg"
    c_faust "Ah, that simplicity and innocence ne’er know\nThemselves, their holy value, and their spell!\nThat meekness, lowliness, the highest graces\nWhich Nature portions out so lovingly—"

translate english jardin_0052:
    pass

translate english jardin_0056:
    voice "voice/jardin_0056.ogg"
    c_margarita "So you but think a moment’s space on me,\nAll times I’ll have to think on you, all places!"

translate english jardin_0060:
    voice "voice/jardin_0060.ogg"
    c_faust "No doubt you’re much alone?"

translate english jardin_0061:
    voice "voice/jardin_0061.ogg"
    c_margarita "Yes, for our household small has grown,\nYet must be cared for, you will own.\nWe have no maid: I do the knitting, sewing, sweeping,\nThe cooking, early work and late, in fact;"
    voice sustain
    c_margarita "And mother, in her notions of housekeeping,\nIs so exact!\nNot that she needs so much to keep expenses down:\nWe, more than others, might take comfort, rather:"
    voice sustain
    c_margarita "A nice estate was left us by my father,\nA house, a little garden near the town.\nBut now my days have less of noise and hurry;\nMy brother is a soldier,"
    voice sustain
    c_margarita "My little sister’s dead.\nTrue, with the child a troubled life I led,\nYet I would take again, and willing, all the worry,\nSo very dear was she."

