    pass

translate english jardin_0105:
    voice "voice/jardin_0105.ogg"
    c_faust "The purest bliss was surely then thy dower."

translate english jardin_0107:
    voice "voice/jardin_0107.ogg"
    c_margarita "But surely, also, many a weary hour.\nI kept the baby’s cradle near\nMy bed at night: if ’t even stirred, I’d guess it,\nAnd waking, hear."
    voice sustain
    c_margarita "And I must nurse it, warm beside me press it,\nAnd oft, to quiet it, my bed forsake,\nAnd dandling back and forth the restless creature take,\nThen at the wash-tub stand, at morning’s break;"
    voice sustain
    c_margarita "And then the marketing and kitchen-tending,\nDay after day, the same thing, never-ending.\nOne’s spirits, Sir, are thus not always good,\nBut then one learns to relish rest and food."

