translate english catedral_0001:
    c_narrator "MARGARET among much people: the EVIL SPIRIT behind MARGARET."

translate english catedral_0002:
    voice "voice/catedral_0002.ogg"
    c_evil_spirit "HOW otherwise was it, Margaret,\nWhen thou, still innocent,\nHere to the altar cam’st,\nAnd from the worn and fingered book"
    voice sustain
    c_evil_spirit "Thy prayers didst prattle,\nHalf sport of childhood,\nHalf God within thee!\nMargaret!"
    voice sustain
    c_evil_spirit "Where tends thy thought?\nWithin thy bosom\nWhat hidden crime?\nPray’st thou for mercy on thy mother’s soul,"
    voice sustain
    c_evil_spirit "That fell asleep to long, long torment, and through thee?\nUpon thy threshold whose the blood?\nAnd stirreth not and quickens\nSomething beneath thy heart,"
    voice sustain
    c_evil_spirit "Thy life disquieting\nWith most foreboding presence?"

