translate english valpurgis_0119:
    voice "voice/valpurgis_0119.ogg"
    c_mephisto "Has not Sir Mammon grandly lighted\nHis palace for this festal night?\n’Tis lucky thou hast seen the sight;\nThe boisterous guests approach that were invited."

translate english valpurgis_0123:
    pass

translate english valpurgis_0125:
    voice "voice/valpurgis_0125.ogg"
    c_faust "How raves the tempest through the air!\nWith what fierce blows upon my neck ’tis beating!"

translate english valpurgis_0127:
    voice "voice/valpurgis_0127.ogg"
    c_mephisto "Under the old ribs of the rock retreating,\nHold fast, lest thou be hurled down the abysses there!\nThe night with the mist is black;\nHark! how the forests grind and crack!"
    voice sustain
    c_mephisto "Frightened, the owlets are scattered:\nHearken! the pillars are shattered.\nThe evergreen palaces shaking!\nBoughs are groaning and breaking,"
    voice sustain
    c_mephisto "The tree-trunks terribly thunder,\nThe roots are twisting asunder!\nIn frightfully intricate crashing\nEach on the other is dashing,"
    voice sustain
    c_mephisto "And over the wreck-strewn gorges\nThe tempest whistles and surges!\nHear’st thou voices higher ringing?\nFar away, or nearer singing?"
    voice sustain
    c_mephisto "Yes, the mountain’s side along,\nSweeps an infuriate glamouring song!"

