translate english valpurgis_0151:
    nvl clear
    voice "voice/valpurgis_0151.ogg"
    c_witches_nvl "The witches ride to the Brocken’s top,\nThe stubble is yellow, and green the crop.\nThere gathers the crowd for carnival:\nSir Urian sits over all."
    nvl clear
    voice sustain
    c_witches_nvl "And so they go over stone and stock;\nThe witch she——s, and——s the buck."

translate english valpurgis_0158:
    nvl clear
    voice "voice/valpurgis_0158.ogg"
    c_voices_nvl "Alone, old Baubo’s coming now;\nShe rides upon a farrow-sow."

translate english valpurgis_0160:
    nvl clear
    voice "voice/valpurgis_0160.ogg"
    c_chorus_nvl "Then honor to whom the honor is due!\nDame Baubo first, to lead the crew!\nA tough old sow and the mother thereon,\nThen follow the witches, every one."

translate english valpurgis_0166:
    nvl clear
    voice "voice/valpurgis_0166.ogg"
    c_voices_nvl "Which way com’st thou hither?"

translate english valpurgis_0167:
    nvl clear
    voice "voice/valpurgis_0167.ogg"
    c_voices_nvl "O’er the Ilsen-stone.\nI peeped at the owl in her nest alone:\nHow she stared and glared!"

translate english valpurgis_0170:
    nvl clear
    c_voices_nvl "Betake thee to Hell!\nWhy so fast and so fell?"

translate english valpurgis_0171:
    nvl clear
    voice "voice/valpurgis_0171.ogg"
    c_voices_nvl "She has scored and has flayed me:\nSee the wounds she has made me!"

translate english valpurgis_0173:
    nvl clear
    voice "voice/valpurgis_0173.ogg"
    c_witches_nvl "The way is wide, the way is long:\nSee, what a wild and crazy throng!\nThe broom it scratches, the fork it thrusts,\nThe child is stifled, the mother bursts."

translate english valpurgis_0179:
    nvl clear
    c_witches_nvl "As doth the snail in shell, we crawl:\nBefore us go the women all.\nWhen towards the Devil’s House we tread,\nWoman’s a thousand steps ahead."

translate english valpurgis_0183:
    nvl clear
    voice "voice/valpurgis_0183.ogg"
    c_witches_nvl "We do not measure with such care:\nWoman in thousand steps is theft.\nBut howsoe’er she hasten may,\nMan in one leap has cleared the way."

translate english valpurgis_0187:
    nvl clear
    voice "voice/valpurgis_0187.ogg"
    c_voices_nvl "Come on, come on, from Rocky Lake!"

translate english valpurgis_0191:
    nvl clear
    voice "voice/valpurgis_0191.ogg"
    c_voices_nvl "Aloft we’d fain ourselves betake.\nWe’ve washed, and are bright as ever you will,\nYet we’re eternally sterile still."

translate english valpurgis_0197:
    nvl clear
    voice "voice/valpurgis_0197.ogg"
    c_witches_nvl "The wind is hushed, the star shoots by.\nThe dreary moon forsakes the sky;\nThe magic notes, like spark on spark,\nDrizzle, whistling through the dark."

translate english valpurgis_0201:
    nvl clear
    c_voices_nvl "Halt, there! Ho, there!"

translate english valpurgis_0202:
    nvl clear
    voice "voice/valpurgis_0202.ogg"
    c_voices_nvl "Who calls from the rocky cleft below there?"

translate english valpurgis_0204:
    nvl clear
    voice "voice/valpurgis_0204.ogg"
    c_voices_nvl "Take me, too! take me, too!\nI’m climbing now three hundred years,\nAnd yet the summit cannot see:\nAmong my equals I would be."

translate english valpurgis_0208:
    nvl clear
    voice "voice/valpurgis_0208.ogg"
    c_witches_nvl "Bears the broom and bears the stock,\nBears the fork and bears the buck:\nWho cannot raise himself to-night\nIs evermore a ruined wight."

translate english valpurgis_0215:
    nvl clear
    voice "voice/valpurgis_0215.ogg"
    c_witches_nvl "So long I stumble, ill bestead,\nAnd the others are now so far ahead!\nAt home I’ve neither rest nor cheer,\nAnd yet I cannot gain them here."

translate english valpurgis_0219:
    nvl clear
    voice "voice/valpurgis_0219.ogg"
    c_witches_nvl "To cheer the witch will salve avail;\nA rag will answer for a sail;\nEach trough a goodly ship supplies;\nHe ne’er will fly, who now not flies."

