translate english valpurgis_0345:
    voice "voice/valpurgis_0345.ogg"
    c_walpurgis_guests "Say, who would put his trust in nations,\nHowe’er for them one may have worked and planned?\nFor with the people, as with women,\nYouth always has the upper hand."

translate english valpurgis_0349:
    voice "voice/valpurgis_0349.ogg"
    c_walpurgis_guests "They’re now too far from what is just and sage.\nI praise the old ones, not unduly:\nWhen we were all-in-all, then, truly,\nThen was the real golden age."

translate english valpurgis_0353:
    voice "voice/valpurgis_0353.ogg"
    c_walpurgis_guests "We also were not stupid, either,\nAnd what we should not, often did;\nBut now all things have from their bases slid,\nJust as we meant to hold them fast together."

translate english valpurgis_0357:
    voice "voice/valpurgis_0357.ogg"
    c_walpurgis_guests "Who, now, a work of moderate sense will read?\nSuch works are held as antiquate and mossy;\nAnd as regards the younger folk, indeed,\nThey never yet have been so pert and saucy."
    voice sustain
    c_narrator "MEPHISTOPHELES (who all at once appears very old)"

translate english valpurgis_0361:
    voice "voice/valpurgis_0361.ogg"
    c_mephisto "I feel that men are ripe for Judgment-Day,\nNow for the last time I’ve the witches’-hill ascended:\nSince to the lees my cask is drained away,\nThe world’s, as well, must soon be ended."

translate english valpurgis_0365:
