translate english valpurgis_0409:
    voice "voice/valpurgis_0409.ogg"
    c_faust "Those two, the old one with the young one sitting,\nThey’ve danced already more than fitting."

translate english valpurgis_0413:
    voice "voice/valpurgis_0413.ogg"
    c_mephisto "No rest to-night for young or old!\nThey start another dance: come now, let us take hold!"

translate english valpurgis_0417:
    voice "voice/valpurgis_0417.ogg"
    c_faust "A lovely dream once came to me;\nI then beheld an apple-tree,\nAnd there two fairest apples shone:\nThey lured me so, I climbed thereon."

translate english valpurgis_0421:
    voice "voice/valpurgis_0421.ogg"
    c_walpurgis_guests "Apples have been desired by you,\nSince first in Paradise they grew;\nAnd I am moved with joy, to know\nThat such within my garden grow."

translate english valpurgis_0425:
    voice "voice/valpurgis_0425.ogg"
    c_mephisto "A dissolute dream once came to me:\nTherein I saw a cloven tree,\nWhich had a————————;\nYet,——as ’twas, I fancied it."

translate english valpurgis_0429:
    voice "voice/valpurgis_0429.ogg"
    c_walpurgis_guests "I offer here my best salute\nUnto the knight with cloven foot!\nLet him a—————prepare,\nIf him—————————does not scare."

translate english valpurgis_0433:
    pass

translate english valpurgis_0434:
    voice "voice/valpurgis_0434.ogg"
    c_walpurgis_guests "Accurséd folk! How dare you venture thus?\nHad you not, long since, demonstration\nThat ghosts can’t stand on ordinary foundation?\nAnd now you even dance, like one of us!"

translate english valpurgis_0438:
    pass

translate english valpurgis_0442:
    voice "voice/valpurgis_0442.ogg"
    c_walpurgis_guests "Why does he come, then, to our ball?"

translate english valpurgis_0444:
    voice "voice/valpurgis_0444.ogg"
    c_faust "O, everywhere on him you fall!\nWhen others dance, he weighs the matter:\nIf he can’t every step bechatter,\nThen ’tis the same as were the step not made;"
    voice sustain
    c_faust "But if you forwards go, his ire is most displayed.\nIf you would whirl in regular gyration\nAs he does in his dull old mill,\nHe’d show, at any rate, good-will,—"
    voice sustain
    c_faust "Especially if you heard and heeded his hortation."
    c_walpurgis_guests "You still are here? Nay, ’tis a thing unheard!\nVanish, at once! We’ve said the enlightening word.\nThe pack of devils by no rules is daunted:\nWe are so wise, and yet is Tegel haunted."
    c_walpurgis_guests "To clear the folly out, how have I swept and stirred!\nTwill ne’er be clean: why, ’tis a thing unheard!"
    c_walpurgis_guests "Then cease to bore us at our ball!"
    c_walpurgis_guests "I tell you, spirits, to your face,\nI give to spirit-despotism no place;\nMy spirit cannot practise it at all."
    c_narrator "The dance continues"

translate english valpurgis_0448:
    pass

translate english valpurgis_0452:
    pass

translate english valpurgis_0456:
    pass

translate english valpurgis_0458:
    voice "voice/valpurgis_0458.ogg"
    c_walpurgis_guests "Naught will succeed, I see, amid such revels;\nYet something from a tour I always save,\nAnd hope, before my last step to the grave,\nTo overcome the poets and the devils."
    c_mephisto "He now will seat him in the nearest puddle;\nThe solace this, whereof he’s most assured:\nAnd when upon his rump the leeches hang and fuddle,\nHe’ll be of spirits and of Spirit cured."
    c_narrator "To FAUST, who has left the dance:"

translate english valpurgis_0462:
    pass

translate english valpurgis_0466:
    c_mephisto "Wherefore forsakest thou the lovely maiden,\nThat in the dance so sweetly sang?"

translate english valpurgis_0469:
    voice "voice/valpurgis_0469.ogg"
    c_faust "Ah! in the midst of it there sprang\nA red mouse from her mouth—sufficient reason."

translate english valpurgis_0470:
    pass

translate english valpurgis_0471:
    voice "voice/valpurgis_0471.ogg"
    c_mephisto "That’s nothing! One must not so squeamish be;\nSo the mouse was not gray, enough for thee.\nWho’d think of that in love’s selected season?"

translate english valpurgis_0475:
    voice "voice/valpurgis_0475.ogg"
    c_faust "Then saw I—."

translate english valpurgis_0476:
    voice "voice/valpurgis_0476.ogg"
    c_mephisto "What?"

translate english valpurgis_0477:
    voice "voice/valpurgis_0477.ogg"
    c_faust "Mephisto, seest thou there,\nAlone and far, a girl most pale and fair?\nShe falters on, her way scarce knowing,\nAs if with fettered feet that stay her going."
    voice sustain
    c_faust "I must confess, it seems to me\nAs if my kindly Margaret were she."

translate english valpurgis_0478:
    pass

translate english valpurgis_0482:
    pass

translate english valpurgis_0485:
    voice "voice/valpurgis_0485.ogg"
    c_mephisto "Let the thing be! All thence have evil drawn:\nIt is a magic shape, a lifeless eidolon.\nSuch to encounter is not good:\nTheir blank, set stare benumbs the human blood,"
    voice sustain
    c_mephisto "And one is almost turned to stone.\nMedusa’s tale to thee is known."

translate english valpurgis_0489:
    pass

translate english valpurgis_0493:
    voice "voice/valpurgis_0493.ogg"
    c_faust "Forsooth, the eyes they are of one whom, dying,\nNo hand with loving pressure closed;\nThat is the breast whereon I once was lying,—\nThe body sweet, beside which I reposed!"

translate english valpurgis_0497:
    pass

translate english valpurgis_0501:
    voice "voice/valpurgis_0501.ogg"
    c_mephisto "Tis magic all, thou fool, seduced so easily!\nUnto each man his love she seems to be."

translate english valpurgis_0505:
    voice "voice/valpurgis_0505.ogg"
    c_faust "The woe, the rapture, so ensnare me,\nThat from her gaze I cannot tear me!\nAnd, strange! around her fairest throat\nA single scarlet band is gleaming,"
    voice sustain
    c_faust "No broader than a knife-blade seeming!"

translate english valpurgis_0509:
    pass

translate english valpurgis_0513:
    voice "voice/valpurgis_0513.ogg"
    c_mephisto "Quite right! The mark I also note.\nHer head beneath her arm she’ll sometimes carry;\nTwas Perseus lopped it, her old adversary.\nThou crav’st the same illusion still!"
    voice sustain
    c_mephisto "Come, let us mount this little hill;\nThe Prater shows no livelier stir,\nAnd, if they’ve not bewitched my sense,\nI verily see a theatre."
    voice sustain
    c_mephisto "What’s going on?"

translate english valpurgis_0517:
    pass

translate english valpurgis_0521:
    pass

translate english valpurgis_0522:
    voice "voice/valpurgis_0522.ogg"
    c_walpurgis_guests "’Twill shortly recommence:\nA new performance—’tis the last of seven.\nTo give that number is the custom here:\n’Twas by a Dilettante written,"
    voice sustain
    c_walpurgis_guests "And Dilettanti in the parts appear.\nThat now I vanish, pardon, I entreat you!\nAs Dilettante I the curtain raise."

translate english valpurgis_0523:
    pass

translate english valpurgis_0527:
    pass

translate english valpurgis_0531:
    voice "voice/valpurgis_0531.ogg"
    c_mephisto "When I upon the Blocksberg meet you,\nI find it good: for that’s your proper place."

translate english intermedio_0001:
    nvl clear
    voice "voice/intermedio_0001.ogg"
    c_dream_figures_nvl "Sons of Mieding, rest to-day!\nNeedless your machinery:\nMisty vale and mountain gray,\nThat is all the scenery."

translate english intermedio_0005:
    nvl clear
    voice "voice/intermedio_0005.ogg"
    c_dream_figures_nvl "That the wedding golden be.\nMust fifty years be rounded:\nBut the Golden give to me,\nWhen the strife’s compounded."

translate english intermedio_0009:
    nvl clear
    voice "voice/intermedio_0009.ogg"
    c_oberon_nvl "Spirits, if you’re here, be seen—\nShow yourselves, delighted!\nFairy king and fairy queen,\nThey are newly plighted."

translate english intermedio_0013:
    nvl clear
    voice "voice/intermedio_0013.ogg"
    c_puck_nvl "Cometh Puck, and, light of limb,\nWhisks and whirls in measure:\nCome a hundred after him,\nTo share with him the pleasure."

translate english intermedio_0017:
    nvl clear
    voice "voice/intermedio_0017.ogg"
    c_ariel_nvl "Ariel’s song is heavenly-pure,\nHis tones are sweet and rare ones:\nThough ugly faces he allure,\nYet he allures the fair ones."

translate english intermedio_0021:
    nvl clear
    voice "voice/intermedio_0021.ogg"
    c_oberon_nvl "Spouses, who would fain agree,\nLearn how we were mated!\nIf your pairs would loving be,\nFirst be separated!"

translate english intermedio_0025:
    nvl clear
    voice "voice/intermedio_0025.ogg"
    c_titania_nvl "If her whims the wife control,\nAnd the man berate her,\nTake him to the Northern Pole,\nAnd her to the Equator!"

translate english intermedio_0029:
    nvl clear
    c_narrator_nvl "Fortissimo."

translate english intermedio_0030:
    nvl clear
    voice "voice/intermedio_0030.ogg"
    c_orchestra_nvl "Snout of fly, mosquito-bill,\nAnd kin of all conditions,\nFrog in grass, and cricket-trill,—\nThese are the musicians!"

translate english intermedio_0034:
    nvl clear
    voice "voice/intermedio_0034.ogg"
    c_orchestra_nvl "See the bagpipe on our track!\n’Tis the soap-blown bubble:\nHear the schnecke-schnicke-schnack\nThrough his nostrils double!"

translate english intermedio_0038:
    nvl clear
    voice "voice/intermedio_0038.ogg"
    c_dream_figures_nvl "Spider’s foot and paunch of toad,\nAnd little wings—we know ’em!\nA little creature ’twill not be,\nBut yet, a little poem."

translate english intermedio_0042:
    nvl clear
    voice "voice/intermedio_0042.ogg"
    c_dream_figures_nvl "Little step and lofty leap\nThrough honey-dew and fragrance:\nYou’ll never mount the airy steep\nWith all your tripping vagrance."

translate english intermedio_0046:
    nvl clear
    voice "voice/intermedio_0046.ogg"
    c_dream_figures_nvl "Is’t but masquerading play?\nSee I with precision?\nOberon, the beauteous fay,\nMeets, to-night, my vision!"

translate english intermedio_0050:
    nvl clear
    c_dream_figures_nvl "Not a claw, no tail I see!\nAnd yet, beyond a cavil,\nLike “the Gods of Greece,” must he\nAlso be a devil."

translate english intermedio_0054:
    nvl clear
    voice "voice/intermedio_0054.ogg"
    c_dream_figures_nvl "I only seize, with sketchy air,\nSome outlines of the tourney;\nYet I betimes myself prepare\nFor my Italian journey."

translate english intermedio_0058:
    nvl clear
    voice "voice/intermedio_0058.ogg"
    c_dream_figures_nvl "My bad luck brings me here, alas!\nHow roars the orgy louder!\nAnd of the witches in the mass,\nBut only two wear powder."

translate english intermedio_0062:
    nvl clear
    voice "voice/intermedio_0062.ogg"
    c_dream_figures_nvl "Powder becomes, like petticoat,\nA gray and wrinkled noddy;\nSo I sit naked on my goat,\nAnd show a strapping body."

translate english intermedio_0066:
    nvl clear
    voice "voice/intermedio_0066.ogg"
    c_dream_figures_nvl "We’ve too much tact and policy\nTo rate with gibes a scolder;\nYet, young and tender though you be,\nI hope to see you moulder."

translate english intermedio_0070:
    nvl clear
    voice "voice/intermedio_0070.ogg"
    c_dream_figures_nvl "Fly-snout and mosquito-bill,\nDon’t swarm so round the Naked!\nFrog in grass and cricket-trill,\nObserve the time, and make it!"

translate english intermedio_0074:
    nvl clear
    c_dream_figures_nvl "Society to one’s desire!\nBrides only, and the sweetest!\nAnd bachelors of youth and fire.\nAnd prospects the completest!"

translate english intermedio_0078:
    nvl clear
    voice "voice/intermedio_0078.ogg"
    c_dream_figures_nvl "And if the Earth don’t open now\nTo swallow up each ranter,\nWhy, then will I myself, I vow,\nJump into hell instanter!"

translate english intermedio_0082:
    nvl clear
    voice "voice/intermedio_0082.ogg"
    c_dream_figures_nvl "Us as little insects see!\nWith sharpest nippers flitting,\nThat our Papa Satan we\nMay honor as is fitting."

translate english intermedio_0086:
    nvl clear
    voice "voice/intermedio_0086.ogg"
    c_dream_figures_nvl "How, in crowds together massed,\nThey are jesting, shameless!\nThey will even say, at last,\nThat their hearts are blameless."

translate english intermedio_0090:
    nvl clear
    voice "voice/intermedio_0090.ogg"
    c_dream_figures_nvl "Among this witches’ revelry\nHis way one gladly loses;\nAnd, truly, it would easier be\nThan to command the Muses."

translate english intermedio_0094:
    nvl clear
    voice "voice/intermedio_0094.ogg"
    c_dream_figures_nvl "The proper folks one’s talents laud:\nCome on, and none shall pass us!\nThe Blocksberg has a summit broad,\nLike Germany’s Parnassus."

translate english intermedio_0098:
    nvl clear
    voice "voice/intermedio_0098.ogg"
    c_dream_figures_nvl "Say, who’s the stiff and pompous man?\nHe walks with haughty paces:\nHe snuffles all he snuffle can:\n“He scents the Jesuits’ traces.”"

translate english intermedio_0102:
    nvl clear
    voice "voice/intermedio_0102.ogg"
    c_dream_figures_nvl "Both clear and muddy streams, for me\nAre good to fish and sport in:\nAnd thus the pious man you see\nWith even devils consorting."

translate english intermedio_0106:
    nvl clear
    voice "voice/intermedio_0106.ogg"
    c_dream_figures_nvl "Yes, for the pious, I suspect,\nAll instruments are fitting;\nAnd on the Blocksberg they erect\nFull many a place of meeting."

translate english intermedio_0110:
    nvl clear
    voice "voice/intermedio_0110.ogg"
    c_dream_figures_nvl "A newer chorus now succeeds!\nI hear the distant drumming.\n“Don’t be disturbed! ’tis, in the reeds,\nThe bittern’s changeless booming.”"

translate english intermedio_0114:
    nvl clear
    voice "voice/intermedio_0114.ogg"
    c_dream_figures_nvl "How each his legs in nimble trip\nLifts up, and makes a clearance!\nThe crooked jump, the heavy skip,\nNor care for the appearance."

translate english intermedio_0118:
    nvl clear
    voice "voice/intermedio_0118.ogg"
    c_dream_figures_nvl "The rabble by such hate are held,\nTo maim and slay delights them:\nAs Orpheus’ lyre the brutes compelled,\nThe bagpipe here unites them."

translate english intermedio_0122:
    nvl clear
    voice "voice/intermedio_0122.ogg"
    c_dream_figures_nvl "I’ll not be led by any lure\nOf doubts or critic-cavils:\nThe Devil must be something, sure,—\nOr how should there be devils?"

translate english intermedio_0126:
    nvl clear
    voice "voice/intermedio_0126.ogg"
    c_dream_figures_nvl "This once, the fancy wrought in me\nIs really too despotic:\nForsooth, if I am all I see,\nI must be idiotic!"

translate english intermedio_0130:
    nvl clear
    voice "voice/intermedio_0130.ogg"
    c_dream_figures_nvl "This racking fuss on every hand,\nIt gives me great vexation;\nAnd, for the first time, here I stand\nOn insecure foundation."

translate english intermedio_0134:
    nvl clear
    voice "voice/intermedio_0134.ogg"
    c_dream_figures_nvl "With much delight I see the play,\nAnd grant to these their merits,\nSince from the devils I also may\nInfer the better spirits."

translate english intermedio_0138:
    nvl clear
    voice "voice/intermedio_0138.ogg"
    c_dream_figures_nvl "The flame they follow, on and on,\nAnd think they’re near the treasure:\nBut Devil rhymes with Doubt alone,\nSo I am here with pleasure."

translate english intermedio_0142:
    nvl clear
    voice "voice/intermedio_0142.ogg"
    c_dream_figures_nvl "Frog in green, and cricket-trill.\nSuch dilettants!—perdition!\nFly-snout and mosquito-bill,—\nEach one’s a fine musician!"

translate english intermedio_0146:
    nvl clear
    voice "voice/intermedio_0146.ogg"
    c_dream_figures_nvl "Sans souci, we call the clan\nOf merry creatures so, then;\nGo a-foot no more we can,\nAnd on our heads we go, then."

translate english intermedio_0150:
    nvl clear
    voice "voice/intermedio_0150.ogg"
    c_dream_figures_nvl "Once many a bit we sponged, but now,\nGod help us! that is done with:\nOur shoes are all danced out, we trow,\nWe’ve but naked soles to run with."

translate english intermedio_0154:
    nvl clear
    voice "voice/intermedio_0154.ogg"
    c_dream_figures_nvl "From the marshes we appear,\nWhere we originated;\nYet in the ranks, at once, we’re here\nAs glittering gallants rated."

translate english intermedio_0158:
    nvl clear
    voice "voice/intermedio_0158.ogg"
    c_dream_figures_nvl "Darting hither from the sky,\nIn star and fire light shooting,\nCross-wise now in grass I lie:\nWho’ll help me to my footing?"

translate english intermedio_0162:
    nvl clear
    voice "voice/intermedio_0162.ogg"
    c_dream_figures_nvl "Room! and round about us, room!\nTrodden are the grasses:\nSpirits also, spirits come,\nAnd they are bulky masses."

translate english intermedio_0166:
    nvl clear
    voice "voice/intermedio_0166.ogg"
    c_puck_nvl "Enter not so stall-fed quite,\nLike elephant-calves about one!\nAnd the heaviest weight to-night\nBe Puck, himself, the stout one!"

translate english intermedio_0170:
    nvl clear
    voice "voice/intermedio_0170.ogg"
    c_ariel_nvl "If loving Nature at your back,\nOr Mind, the wings uncloses,\nFollow up my airy track\nTo the mount of roses!"

translate english intermedio_0174:
    nvl clear
    voice "voice/intermedio_0174.ogg"
    c_orchestra_nvl "pianissimo\nCloud and trailing mist o’erhead\nAre now illuminated:\nAir in leaves, and wind in reed,\nAnd all is dissipated."

translate english dia_nebuloso_0001:
    c_narrator "A FIELD\nFAUST MEPHISTOPHELES"

translate english dia_nebuloso_0002:
    voice "voice/dia_nebuloso_0002.ogg"
    c_faust "In misery! In despair! Long wretchedly astray on the face of the earth, and now imprisoned! That gracious, ill-starred creature shut in a dungeon as a criminal, and given up to fearful torments! To this has it come! to this!—"
    voice sustain
    c_faust "Treacherous, contemptible spirit, and thou hast concealed it from me!—Stand, then,—stand! Roll the devilish eyes wrathfully in thy head! Stand and defy me with thine intolerable presence! Imprisoned! In irretrievable misery! Delivered up to evil spirits, and to condemning, unfeeling Man!"
    voice sustain
    c_faust "And thou hast lulled me, meanwhile, with the most insipid dissipations, hast concealed from me her increasing wretchedness, and suffered her to go helplessly to ruin!"

translate english dia_nebuloso_0003:
    pass

translate english dia_nebuloso_0004:
    pass

translate english dia_nebuloso_0005:
    voice "voice/dia_nebuloso_0005.ogg"
    c_mephisto "She is not the first."

translate english dia_nebuloso_0006:
    voice "voice/dia_nebuloso_0006.ogg"
    c_faust "Dog! Abominable monster! Transform him, thou Infinite Spirit! transform the reptile again into his dog-shape?"
    voice sustain
    c_faust "in which it pleased him often at night to scamper on before me, to roll himself at the feet of the unsuspecting wanderer, and hang upon his shoulders when he fell!"
    voice sustain
    c_faust "Transform him again into his favorite likeness, that he may crawl upon his belly in the dust before me,—that I may trample him, the outlawed, under foot! Not the first! O woe!"
    voice sustain
    c_faust "woe which no human soul can grasp, that more than one being should sink into the depths of this misery,—that the first, in its writhing death-agony under the eyes of the Eternal Forgiver, did not expiate the guilt of all others!"
    voice sustain
    c_faust "The misery of this single one pierces to the very marrow of my life; and thou art calmly grinning at the fate of thousands!"

translate english dia_nebuloso_0007:
    pass

translate english dia_nebuloso_0008:
    pass

translate english dia_nebuloso_0009:
    pass

translate english dia_nebuloso_0010:
    voice "voice/dia_nebuloso_0010.ogg"
    c_mephisto "Now we are already again at the end of our wits, where the understanding of you men runs wild. Why didst thou enter into fellowship with us, if thou canst not carry it out? Wilt fly, and art not secure against dizziness?"
    voice sustain
    c_mephisto "Did we thrust ourselves upon thee, or thou thyself upon us?"

translate english dia_nebuloso_0011:
    voice "voice/dia_nebuloso_0011.ogg"
    c_faust "Gnash not thus thy devouring teeth at me? It fills me with horrible disgust."
    voice sustain
    c_faust "Mighty, glorious Spirit, who hast vouchsafed to me Thine apparition, who knowest my heart and my soul, why fetter me to the felon-comrade, who feeds on mischief and gluts himself with ruin?"

translate english dia_nebuloso_0012:
    pass

translate english dia_nebuloso_0013:
    voice "voice/dia_nebuloso_0013.ogg"
    c_mephisto "Hast thou done?"

translate english dia_nebuloso_0014:
    voice "voice/dia_nebuloso_0014.ogg"
    c_faust "Rescue her, or woe to thee! The fearfullest curse be upon thee for thousands of ages!"

translate english dia_nebuloso_0015:
    voice "voice/dia_nebuloso_0015.ogg"
    c_mephisto "I cannot loosen the bonds of the Avenger, nor undo his bolts. Rescue her? Who was it that plunged her into ruin? I, or thou?"

translate english dia_nebuloso_0016:
    pass

translate english dia_nebuloso_0017:
    pass

translate english dia_nebuloso_0018:
    voice sustain
    c_narrator "FAUST looks around wildly."

translate english dia_nebuloso_0019:
    voice sustain
    c_mephisto "Wilt thou grasp the thunder? Well that it has not been given to you, miserable mortals! To crush to pieces the innocent respondent—that is the tyrant-fashion of relieving one’s self in embarrassments."

translate english dia_nebuloso_0020:
    voice "voice/dia_nebuloso_0020.ogg"
    c_faust "Take me thither! She shall be free!"

translate english dia_nebuloso_0021:
    voice "voice/dia_nebuloso_0021.ogg"
    c_mephisto "And the danger to which thou wilt expose thyself? Know that the guilt of blood, from thy hand, still lies upon the town! Avenging spirits hover over the spot where the victim fell, and lie in wait for the returning murderer."

translate english dia_nebuloso_0022:
    voice "voice/dia_nebuloso_0022.ogg"
    c_faust "That, too, from thee? Murder and death of a world upon thee, monster! Take me thither, I say, and liberate her!"

translate english dia_nebuloso_0023:
    voice "voice/dia_nebuloso_0023.ogg"
    c_mephisto "I will convey thee there; and hear, what I can do! Have I all the power in Heaven and on Earth? I will becloud the jailer’s senses: get possession of the key, and lead her forth with human hand!"
    voice sustain
    c_mephisto "I will keep watch: the magic steeds are ready, I will carry you off. So much is in my power."

translate english dia_nebuloso_0024:
    voice "voice/dia_nebuloso_0024.ogg"
    c_faust "Up and away!"

translate english noche_campo_0001:
    c_narrator "FAUST and MEPHISTOPHELES speeding onward on black horses."

translate english noche_campo_0002:
    voice "voice/noche_campo_0002.ogg"
    c_faust "What weave they there round the raven-stone?"

translate english noche_campo_0003:
    voice "voice/noche_campo_0003.ogg"
    c_mephisto "I know not what they are brewing and doing."

translate english noche_campo_0004:
    voice "voice/noche_campo_0004.ogg"
    c_faust "Soaring up, sweeping down, bowing and bending!"

translate english noche_campo_0005:
    c_mephisto "A witches’-guild."

translate english noche_campo_0006:
    voice "voice/noche_campo_0006.ogg"
    c_faust "They scatter, devote and doom!"

translate english noche_campo_0007:
    voice "voice/noche_campo_0007.ogg"
    c_mephisto "On! on!"

translate english carcel_0002:
    c_narrator "FAUST (with a bunch of keys and a lamp, before an iron door)"
    c_faust "A shudder, long unfelt, comes o’er me;\nMankind’s collected woe o’erwhelms me, here.\nShe dwells within the dark, damp walls before me,\nAnd all her crime was a delusion dear!"
    c_faust "What! I delay to free her?\nI dread, once again to see her?\nOn! my shrinking but lingers Death more near."

translate english carcel_0006:
    pass

translate english carcel_0010:
    pass

translate english carcel_0012:
    pass

translate english carcel_0013:
    c_narrator "He grasps the lock: the sound of singing is heard inside."

translate english carcel_0014:
    c_faust "My mother, the harlot,\nWho put me to death;\nMy father, the varlet,\nWho eaten me hath!"
    c_faust "Little sister, so good,\nLaid my bones in the wood,\nIn the damp moss and clay:\nThen was I a beautiful bird o’ the wood;"
    c_faust "Fly away! Fly away!"

