    pass

translate english carcel_0022:
    pass

translate english carcel_0025:
    voice "voice/carcel_0025.ogg"
    c_faust "She does not dream her lover listens near;\nThat he the rattling chain, the rustling straw, can hear."

translate english carcel_0028:
    voice sustain
    c_narrator "He enters."

translate english carcel_0029:
    voice "voice/carcel_0029.ogg"
    c_margarita "Woe! woe! They come. O death of bitterness!"

translate english carcel_0030:
    pass

translate english carcel_0031:
    voice "voice/carcel_0031.ogg"
    c_faust "Hush! hush! The hour is come that frees thee."

translate english carcel_0032:
    pass

translate english carcel_0033:
    voice "voice/carcel_0033.ogg"
    c_margarita "Art thou a man, then pity my distress!"

translate english carcel_0034:
    pass

translate english carcel_0035:
    voice "voice/carcel_0035.ogg"
    c_faust "Thy cries will wake the guards, and they will seize thee!"

translate english carcel_0036:
    pass

translate english carcel_0037:
    voice sustain
    c_narrator "He takes hold of the fetters to unlock them."

translate english carcel_0038:
    voice "voice/carcel_0038.ogg"
    c_margarita "Who, headsman! unto thee such power\nOver me could give?\nThou’rt come for me at midnight-hour:\nHave mercy on me, let me live!"
    voice sustain
    c_margarita "Is’t not soon enough when morning chime has run?"

translate english carcel_0042:
    pass

translate english carcel_0043:
    voice sustain
    c_narrator "She rises."

translate english carcel_0044:
    voice sustain
    c_margarita "And I am yet so young, so young!\nAnd now Death comes, and ruin!\nI, too, was fair, and that was my undoing.\nMy love was near, but now he’s far;"
    voice sustain
    c_margarita "Torn lies the wreath, scattered the blossoms are.\nSeize me not thus so violently!\nSpare me! What have I done to thee?\nLet me not vainly entreat thee!"
    voice sustain
    c_margarita "I never chanced, in all my days, to meet thee!"

translate english carcel_0048:
    pass

translate english carcel_0052:
    pass

translate english carcel_0054:
    voice "voice/carcel_0054.ogg"
    c_faust "Shall I outlive this misery?"

translate english carcel_0055:
    pass

translate english carcel_0056:
    voice "voice/carcel_0056.ogg"
    c_margarita "Now am I wholly in thy might.\nBut let me suckle, first, my baby!\nI blissed it all this livelong night;\nThey took ’t away, to vex me, maybe,"
    voice sustain
    c_margarita "And now they say I killed the child outright.\nAnd never shall I be glad again.\nThey sing songs about me! ’tis bad of the folk to do it!\nThere’s an old story has the same refrain;"
    voice sustain
    c_margarita "Who bade them so construe it?"

translate english carcel_0057:
    pass

translate english carcel_0061:
    pass

translate english carcel_0065:
    pass

translate english carcel_0066:
    voice "voice/carcel_0066.ogg"
    c_faust "Here lieth one who loves thee ever,\nThe thraldom of thy woe to sever."

translate english carcel_0068:
    voice "voice/carcel_0068.ogg"
    c_margarita "O let us kneel, and call the Saints to hide us!\nUnder the steps beside us,\nThe threshold under,\nHell heaves in thunder!"
    voice sustain
    c_margarita "The Evil One\nWith terrible wrath\nSeeketh a path\nHis prey to discover!"

translate english carcel_0072:
    pass

translate english carcel_0073:
    c_faust "Margaret! Margaret!"

translate english carcel_0074:
    voice "voice/carcel_0074.ogg"
    c_margarita "That was the voice of my lover!"

translate english carcel_0075:
    voice sustain
    c_narrator "She springs to her feet: the fetters fall off."

translate english carcel_0076:
    voice sustain
    c_margarita "Where is he? I heard him call me.\nI am free! No one shall enthrall me.\nTo his neck will I fly,\nOn his bosom lie!"
    voice sustain
    c_margarita "On the threshold he stood, and Margaret! calling,\nMidst of Hell’s howling and noises appalling,\nMidst of the wrathful, infernal derision,\nI knew the sweet sound of the voice of the vision!"

translate english carcel_0080:
    pass

translate english carcel_0084:
    voice "voice/carcel_0084.ogg"
    c_faust "’Tis I!"
    c_margarita "’Tis thou! O, say it once again!"
    c_narrator "Clasping him."

translate english carcel_0085:
    voice "voice/carcel_0085.ogg"
    c_margarita "’Tis he! ’tis he! Where now is all my pain?\nThe anguish of the dungeon, and the chain?\n’Tis thou! Thou comest to save me,\nAnd I am saved!—"
    voice sustain
    c_margarita "Again the street I see\nWhere first I looked on thee;\nAnd the garden, brightly blooming,\nWhere I and Martha wait thy coming."

translate english carcel_0086:
    pass

translate english carcel_0090:
    pass

translate english carcel_0094:
    voice "voice/carcel_0094.ogg"
    c_faust "Come! Come with me!"

translate english carcel_0095:
    voice "voice/carcel_0095.ogg"
    c_margarita "Delay, now!\nSo fain I stay, when thou delayest!"
    voice sustain
    c_narrator "Caressing him."

translate english carcel_0096:
    pass

translate english carcel_0097:
    voice "voice/carcel_0097.ogg"
    c_faust "Away, now!\nIf longer here thou stayest,\nWe shall be made to dearly rue it."

translate english carcel_0098:
    pass

translate english carcel_0099:
    voice "voice/carcel_0099.ogg"
    c_margarita "Kiss me!—canst no longer do it?\nMy friend, so short a time thou’rt missing,\nAnd hast unlearned thy kissing?\nWhy is my heart so anxious, on thy breast?"
    voice sustain
    c_margarita "Where once a heaven thy glances did create me,\nA heaven thy loving words expressed,\nAnd thou didst kiss, as thou wouldst suffocate me—\nKiss me!"
    voice sustain
    c_margarita "Or I’ll kiss thee!"

translate english carcel_0100:
    pass

translate english carcel_0104:
    pass

translate english carcel_0108:
    pass

translate english carcel_0109:
    voice sustain
    c_narrator "She embraces him."

translate english carcel_0110:
    voice sustain
    c_margarita "Ah, woe! thy lips are chill,\nAnd still.\nHow changed in fashion\nThy passion!"
    voice sustain
    c_margarita "Who has done me this ill?"

translate english carcel_0112:
    voice sustain
    c_narrator "She turns away from him."

translate english carcel_0113:
    voice "voice/carcel_0113.ogg"
    c_faust "Come, follow me! My darling, be more bold:\nI’ll clasp thee, soon, with warmth a thousand-fold;\nBut follow now! ’Tis all I beg of thee."

translate english carcel_0116:
    voice "voice/carcel_0116.ogg"
    c_margarita "And is it thou? Thou, surely, certainly?"

translate english carcel_0117:
    voice "voice/carcel_0117.ogg"
    c_faust "’Tis I! Come on!"

translate english carcel_0118:
    voice "voice/carcel_0118.ogg"
    c_margarita "Thou wilt unloose my chain,\nAnd in thy lap wilt take me once again.\nHow comes it that thou dost not shrink from me?—\nSay, dost thou know, my friend, whom thou mak’st free?"

translate english carcel_0119:
    pass

translate english carcel_0122:
    voice "voice/carcel_0122.ogg"
    c_faust "Come! come! The night already vanisheth."

translate english carcel_0124:
    voice "voice/carcel_0124.ogg"
    c_margarita "My mother have I put to death;\nI’ve drowned the baby born to thee.\nWas it not given to thee and me?\nThee, too!—’Tis thou! It scarcely true doth seem—"
    voice sustain
    c_margarita "Give me thy hand! ’Tis not a dream!\nThy dear, dear hand!—But, ah, ’tis wet!\nWhy, wipe it off! Methinks that yet\nThere’s blood thereon."
    voice sustain
    c_margarita "Ah, God! what hast thou done?\nNay, sheathe thy sword at last!\nDo not affray me!"

translate english carcel_0125:
    pass

translate english carcel_0129:
    pass

translate english carcel_0133:
    pass

translate english carcel_0134:
    voice "voice/carcel_0134.ogg"
    c_faust "O, let the past be past!\nThy words will slay me!"

translate english carcel_0135:
    pass

translate english carcel_0137:
    voice "voice/carcel_0137.ogg"
    c_margarita "No, no! Thou must outlive us.\nNow I’ll tell thee the graves to give us:\nThou must begin to-morrow\nThe work of sorrow!"
    voice sustain
    c_margarita "The best place give to my mother,\nThen close at her side my brother,\nAnd me a little away,\nBut not too very far, I pray!"
    voice sustain
    c_margarita "And here, on my right breast, my baby lay!\nNobody else will lie beside me!—\nAh, within thine arms to hide me,\nThat was a sweet and a gracious bliss,"
    voice sustain
    c_margarita "But no more, no more can I attain it!\nI would force myself on thee and constrain it,\nAnd it seems thou repellest my kiss:\nAnd yet ’tis thou, so good, so kind to see!"

