    pass

translate english carcel_0154:
    voice "voice/carcel_0154.ogg"
    c_faust "If thou feel’st it is I, then come with me!"

translate english carcel_0155:
    c_margarita "Out yonder?"

translate english carcel_0156:
    voice "voice/carcel_0156.ogg"
    c_faust "To freedom."

translate english carcel_0157:
    voice "voice/carcel_0157.ogg"
    c_margarita "If the grave is there,\nDeath lying in wait, then come!\nFrom here to eternal rest:\nNo further step—no, no!"
    voice sustain
    c_margarita "Thou goest away! O Henry, if I could go!"

translate english carcel_0158:
    pass

translate english carcel_0162:
    pass

translate english carcel_0163:
    voice "voice/carcel_0163.ogg"
    c_faust "Thou canst! Just will it! Open stands the door."

translate english carcel_0164:
    pass

translate english carcel_0165:
    voice "voice/carcel_0165.ogg"
    c_margarita "I dare not go: there’s no hope any more.\nWhy should I fly? They’ll still my steps waylay!\nIt is so wretched, forced to beg my living,\nAnd a bad conscience sharper misery giving!"
    voice sustain
    c_margarita "It is so wretched, to be strange, forsaken,\nAnd I’d still be followed and taken!"

translate english carcel_0166:
    pass

translate english carcel_0170:
    pass

translate english carcel_0172:
    voice "voice/carcel_0172.ogg"
    c_faust "I’ll stay with thee."

translate english carcel_0173:
    voice "voice/carcel_0173.ogg"
    c_margarita "Be quick! Be quick!\nSave thy perishing child!\nAway! Follow the ridge\nUp by the brook,"
    voice sustain
    c_margarita "Death lying in wait, then come!]"
    voice sustain
    c_margarita "Over the bridge,\nInto the wood,\nTo the left, where the plank is placed\nIn the pool!"
    voice sustain
    c_margarita "Seize it in haste!\n’Tis trying to rise,\n’Tis struggling still!\nSave it! Save it!"

translate english carcel_0174:
    pass

translate english carcel_0178:
    pass

translate english carcel_0180:
    voice "voice/carcel_0180.ogg"
    c_faust "Recall thy wandering will!\nOne step, and thou art free at last!"

translate english carcel_0181:
    voice "voice/carcel_0181.ogg"
    c_margarita "If the mountain we had only passed!\nThere sits my mother upon a stone,—\nI feel an icy shiver!\nThere sits my mother upon a stone,"
    voice sustain
    c_margarita "And her head is wagging ever.\nShe beckons, she nods not, her heavy head falls o’er;\nShe slept so long that she wakes no more.\nShe slept, while we were caressing:"
    voice sustain
    c_margarita "Ah, those were the days of blessing!"

